Python remains readable for beginners compared to Java primarily due to its concise and straightforward syntax. For example, the 'Hello, World!' program in Python is written in a single line: `print("Hello, World!")`. In contrast, the equivalent program in Java requires five lines of code:

```java
public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```
This simplicity in Python's syntax makes it easier for beginners to understand and write code without getting overwhelmed by complex structures [openstax-py-ch01_p06_para_02][openstax-py-ch01_p06_para_03].
